                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirichlet+character"} Dirichlet character
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %math#mathml_63e4a3bd826a49ac3b8e2f5d66fe97285439ca4c_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi z
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{z} = 0
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+L-function"} Artin L-function
                    of a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+representation"} Galois representation
                    %math#mathml_63e4a3bd826a49ac3b8e2f5d66fe97285439ca4c_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{z}
                    , expressible “in coordinates” (via
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+reciprocity"} Artin reciprocity
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirichlet+L-function"} Dirichlet L-function
                    (for 1-dimensional Galois representations) and generally (via
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+correspondence"} Langlands correspondence
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphic+L-function"} automorphic L-function
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
          %h2#references References
          %p The original article is
          %ul
            %li#Selberg56
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atle+Selberg"}> Atle Selberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Harmonic analysis and discontinuous groups in weakly symmetric Riemannian spaces with applications to Dirichlet series
          %p Review includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selberg_zeta_function"} Selberg zeta function
            %li#Watkins
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Watkins"}> Matthew Watkins
                , citation collection on
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://empslocal.ex.ac.uk/people/staff/mrwatkin/zeta/physics4.htm"} Selberg trace formula and zeta functions
            %li#Bump
              %p
                Bump, below theorem 19 in
                %em
                  Spectral theory of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo \
                        %mi SL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \backslash SL(2,\mathbb{R})
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BumpSpectralTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %em Selberg and Ruelle zeta functions for compact hyperbolic manifolds
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/people/xenia/Oberseminar%202014/Oberseminar%202014.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            Expression of the Selberg/Ruelle zeta function as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+product"} Euler product
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+polynomials"} characteristic polynomials
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Gangolli77
              %p
                Ramesh Gangolli,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Zeta functions of Selberg’s type for compact space forms of symmetric spaces of rank one
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.ijm/1256049498"} Euclid
            %li#Fried86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Fried"}> David Fried
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The zeta functions of Ruelle and Selberg. I
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=ASENS_1986_4_19_4_491_0"} Numdam
          %p
            The analogy with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+L-function"} Artin L-function
            is highlighted in
          %ul
            %li#Brown09
              %p
                Darin Brown,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lifting properties of prime geodesics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.rmjm/1239113439"} euclid
            %li#Morishita12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masanori+Morishita"}> Masanori Morishita
                , section 12.1 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Knots and Primes: An Introduction to Arithmetic Topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=DOnkGOTnI78C&pg=PA156#v=onepage&q&f=false"} web
          %p
            Discussion of the relation between, on the one hand,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+function+of+an+elliptic+differential+operator"} zeta function
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laplace+operators"} Laplace operators
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eta+function+of+a+self-adjoint+operator"} eta funcstions
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operators"} Dirac operators
            and, on the other hand, Selberg zeta functions includes
          %ul
            %li#DHokerPhong86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+D%27Hoker"} Eric D'Hoker
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duong+Phong"} Duong Phong
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Communications in Mathematical Physics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104115166"} Euclid
            %li#Sarnak87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Sarnak"}> Peter Sarnak
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Determinants of Laplacians
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104159171"} Euclid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Olbrich"} Martin Olbrich
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The wave kernel for the Laplacian on the classical locally symmetric spaces of rank one, theta functions, trace formulas and the Selberg zeta function
            %li#BunkeOlbrich94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                , Martin Olbrich,
                %em Theta and zeta functions for locally symmetric spaces of rank one
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/dg-ga/9407013"}> arXiv:dg-ga/9407013
                )
          %p and for odd-dimensional spaces also in
          %ul
            %li#Fried86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Fried"}> David Fried
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Analytic torsion and closed geodesics on hyperbolic manifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://gdz-lucene.tc.sub.uni-goettingen.de/gcs/gcs?&&action=pdf&metsFile=PPN356556735_0084&divID=LOG_0026&pagesize=original&pdfTitlePage=http://gdz.sub.uni-goettingen.de/dms/load/pdftitle/?metsFile=PPN356556735_0084%7C&targetFileName=PPN356556735_0084_LOG_0026.pdf&"} pdf
            %li#Millson78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Millson"}> John Millson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Closed geodesic and the
                    = succeed "-invariant" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi η
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1970928"} jstor
            %li#BunkeOlbrich94a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Olbrich"} Martin Olbrich
                %em Theta and zeta functions for odd-dimensional locally symmetric spaces of rank one
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/dg-ga/9407012"}> arXiv:dg-ga/9407012
                )
            %li#BunkeOlbrich94b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Olbrich"} Martin Olbrich
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                  \-Cohomology and the Selbeg zeta function
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/dg-ga/9411004"}> arXiv:dg-ga/9411004
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Olbrich"} Martin Olbrich
                %em Group cohomology and the singularities of the Selberg zeta function associated to a Kleinian group
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/dg-ga/9603003"}> arXiv:dg-ga/9603003
                )
            %li#BunkeOlbrich95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Olbrich"} Martin Olbrich
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Selberg zeta and theta functions: a differential operator approach
            %li#Park01
              %p
                Jinsung Park,
                %em Eta invariants and regularized determinants for odd dimensional hyperbolic manifolds with cusps
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0111175"}> arXiv:0111175
                )
            %li#Friedman04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joshua+Friedman"}> Joshua Friedman
                ,
                %em The Selberg trace formula and Selberg zeta-function for cofinite Kleinian groups with finite-dimensional unitary representations
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0410067"}> arXiv:math/0410067
                )
            %li#Friedman06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joshua+Friedman"}> Joshua Friedman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Regularized determinants of the Laplacian for cofinite Kleinian groups with finite-dimensional unitary representations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0605288"} arXiv:math/0605288
            %li#GuillarmouMoroianuPark09
              %p
                Colin Guillarmou, Sergiu Moroianu, Jinsung Park,
                %em Eta invariant and Selberg Zeta function of odd type over convex co-compact hyperbolic manifolds
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0901.4082"}> arXiv:0901.4082
                )
